{"items":[{"created_at":"2026-08-23T22:12:07.899128+00:00","text":"User request:\nWhats the weather lik in vegas?\n\nOBus answer:\nLas Vegas is **hot and sunny today**—around **100°F**, with a high near **109°F** and a low around **85–86°F** tonight. Winds may reach **10–20 mph**. Stay hydrated and limit midday outdoor activity. ([NWS forecast](https://[[AUTHORIZATION REDACTED]]/MapClick.php?FcstType=text&lat=36.0889&lg=english&lon=-115.163), [current conditions](https://[[AUTHORIZATION REDACTED]]/weather/forecast/NV/Las%2BVegas))","tags":["conversation","auto","local-moa-router-luna-aggregate"],"source":"auto-route","id":"mem-11cf067bd1c9ac7f68f8"},{"created_at":"2026-08-23T22:12:47.590808+00:00","text":"User request:\nAnswer the user's request directly in plain text.\n\nuser: Prompts run the Obus are slow in teh ap\n\nOBus answer:\nIf prompts in the OBus app are slow, the most common causes are:\n\n1. The request is being sent to a remote or overloaded provider.\n2. The selected model is too large for your hardware.\n3. Routing adds unnecessary processing steps.\n4. Ollama or the local model is not running efficiently.\n5. The prompt or conversation history is very long.\n\nTry these checks:\n\n- Confirm which provider and model handled the request.\n- Test a short prompt in a new conversation.\n- Select a smaller, faster model.\n- Verify Ollama is running and the model is loaded locally.\n- Check CPU, RAM, GPU, and VRAM usage while generating.\n- Disable unnecessary routing or fallback layers temporarily.\n- Restart the OBus app and Ollama service.\n- Compare response time with the same prompt directly in Ollama.\n\nIf only long conversations are slow, start a new chat or reduce the context/history being sent. If every prompt is slow, the issue is more likely routing, provider availability, or local resource limits.","tags":["conversation","auto","local-moa-router-luna-aggregate"],"source":"auto-route","id":"mem-b37258d024951547127d"},{"created_at":"2026-08-23T22:13:16.109493+00:00","text":"User request:\nAnswer the user's request directly in plain text.\n\nuser: Prompts run the Obus are slow in teh ap\n\nOBus answer:\nOBus prompts may be slow because of provider throttling, network latency, large prompts, or routing through a busy model.\n\nTry these fixes:\n\n- Switch from a free/limited provider to a local Ollama model, if available.\n- Shorten the prompt and reduce unnecessary context.\n- Disable VPN or test your network connection.\n- Check whether OBUS is routing requests through a rate-limited provider.\n- Prefer a local, ready, warmed-up model for quick tasks.\n- Restart the app or send one small warm-up prompt.\n\nIf only certain prompts are slow, their size or complexity is probably the main cause.","tags":["conversation","auto","local-moa-router-luna-aggregate"],"source":"auto-route","id":"mem-0de0ecd45a0bd24a7134"},{"created_at":"2026-08-23T22:13:37.215463+00:00","text":"User request:\nAnswer the user's request directly in plain text.\n\nuser: Prompts run the Obus are slow in teh ap\n\nOBus answer:\nIf prompts in the OBus app are running slowly, try these steps:\n\n1. Test a new chat with a short prompt such as “Hello.”\n   - If it’s fast, the original conversation may have too much history. Start a new chat or remove older messages.\n\n2. Check the selected provider and model.\n   - Larger models are slower. Try a smaller or faster model temporarily.\n\n3. If using Ollama:\n   - Confirm Ollama is running.\n   - Make sure the model is loaded and fits in available RAM/VRAM.\n   - Check CPU, memory, GPU, and VRAM usage.\n   - Smaller quantized models usually respond faster.\n   - Keep the model loaded if possible to avoid delays from repeated loading.\n\n4. Check your connection if using a cloud provider.\n   - Slow network, service congestion, or rate limits can add latency.\n\n5. Restart OBus and Ollama, then test again.\n\nIf even a short prompt is consistently slow, the likely causes are the selected model, insufficient hardware, or provider/server latency.","tags":["conversation","auto","local-moa-router-luna-aggregate"],"source":"auto-route","id":"mem-53036e980b4081a33b4d"},{"created_at":"2026-08-23T22:13:44.369602+00:00","text":"User request:\nAnswer the user's request directly in plain text.\n\nuser: Prompts run the Obus are slow in teh ap\n\nOBus answer:\nPrompts in the OBus app can be slow for several reasons:\n\n- The selected provider or model may be overloaded.\n- A large model may be running slowly on your hardware.\n- OBus may be using routing, fallback, or multiple processing steps.\n- Ollama may not be running correctly, causing a fallback to another provider.\n- A long conversation history or large prompt may increase processing time.\n\nTry these quick checks:\n\n1. Test a short prompt in a new conversation.\n2. Check which provider and model OBus is using.\n3. Try a smaller or faster model.\n4. If using Ollama, run `ollama ps` to confirm the model is loaded and `ollama list` to confirm it is installed.\n5. Temporarily disable routing or fallback options.\n6. Compare response speed with Ollama directly and with another provider.\n\nIf every prompt is slow, the issue is likely provider, network, or app overhead. If only long prompts are slow, reduce the conversation history or prompt size.","tags":["conversation","auto","local-moa-router-luna-aggregate"],"source":"auto-route","id":"mem-0a1332586019facc0371"},{"created_at":"2026-08-23T22:14:13.348766+00:00","text":"User request:\nAnswer the user's request directly in plain text.\n\nuser: Prompts run the Obus are slow in teh ap\n\nOBus answer:\nPrompts in the OBus app may be slow because of the model, long chat history, network latency, or limited system resources.\n\nTry these steps:\n\n1. Send a short prompt like “Hello” in a new chat.\n2. If you use Ollama, make sure the model is loaded and running locally. Larger models need more RAM/VRAM and respond more slowly.\n3. Reduce the prompt and conversation history.\n4. Check CPU, RAM, GPU, and VRAM usage while generating.\n5. Restart OBus and Ollama.\n6. Disable VPNs or proxies and check your connection.\n7. Try a smaller or faster model.\n\nIf short prompts are also slow, the likely causes are model loading, insufficient hardware, or the selected provider/API throttling requests.","tags":["conversation","auto","local-moa-router-luna-aggregate"],"source":"auto-route","id":"mem-9e7706fb2eec0661f1c0"},{"created_at":"2026-08-23T22:14:44.704815+00:00","text":"User request:\nAnswer the user's request directly in plain text.\n\nuser: Prompts run the Obus are slow in teh ap\n\nOBus answer:\nIf prompts run slowly in the OBus app, try these checks:\n\n1. Send a very short prompt like “Hello” in a new chat. If that is fast, the conversation history or prompt size is likely the cause.\n2. Start a new chat or reduce the amount of attached context and previous messages.\n3. Check which model and provider OBus is using. Local Ollama models may be faster than cloud or fallback routes, depending on your hardware.\n4. Confirm Ollama is running and monitor CPU, GPU, RAM, and VRAM usage. Insufficient resources can slow generation.\n5. Disable VPNs or proxies temporarily and remove unnecessary routing or fallback providers.\n6. Restart both OBus and Ollama.\n7. Run the same prompt directly through Ollama. If it is fast there, the delay is probably in OBus or its integration.\n\nIf the issue continues, note the model, provider, operating system, prompt size, and whether the delay occurs before generation starts or while tokens are being produced. These details will help identify whether the bottleneck is context processing, hardware, networking, or the OBus integration.","tags":["conversation","auto","local-moa-router-luna-aggregate"],"source":"auto-route","id":"mem-6fb5737bf95929a393c2"},{"created_at":"2026-08-23T22:15:13.228254+00:00","text":"User request:\nAnswer the user's request directly in plain text.\n\nuser: Prompts run the Obus are